<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Cookie policy</h1>
<p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600">
  The short version: nothing beyond the essentials runs until you say yes, your
  choice is remembered across our sites, and you can change it any time on this
  page.
</p>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-400">
  Applies to growcentric.ai and app.growcentric.ai, operated by Keferboeck Ltd.
  Last updated 12 August 2026.
</p>

<div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600">
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">What cookies are</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Cookies are small text files a website stores in your browser. Some are
      needed for a site to work at all, for example to keep you signed in.
      Others help us understand how the site is used or whether our advertising
      works. Only the first kind runs without your consent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">How your choice works across our sites</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      GrowCentric runs on two addresses: the website at growcentric.ai and this
      app. When you accept cookies on either one, we store your consent for
      both, so you are not asked twice. When you decline, we remember that only
      on the site where you declined, and we also withdraw any earlier
      acceptance. The other site will ask you fresh. Declining is remembered
      for six months, accepting for twelve.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Essential cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">These make the sites work and need no consent.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-gray-950/5">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[32rem] text-left">
        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-gray-950">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Cookie</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Lifetime</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 bg-white">
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-950">gc_cookie_consent</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Remembers your cookie choice for our sites.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">12 months, 6 if declined</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-950">_growcentric_session</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Keeps you signed in during a visit and protects forms against cross site request forgery. Also stores your language choice.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">Until the browser closes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-950">remember_user_token</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Set when you tick "Keep me signed in" so you stay logged in between visits.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">About 2 weeks</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Analytics cookies (only with your consent)</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages help and which
      confuse. IP addresses are anonymized by Google Analytics by design.
      The cookies are <span class="font-mono text-xs">_ga</span> and
      <span class="font-mono text-xs">_ga_*</span>, each living up to 2 years.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We also use Fathom Analytics, which is cookieless and stores no personal
      data at all. It runs without consent because it has nothing to consent
      to: no cookies, no identifiers, no cross site tracking, servers in the EU.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Marketing cookies (only with your consent)</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We advertise on Google and on LinkedIn. Google Ads sets
      <span class="font-mono text-xs">_gcl_au</span> (3 months) to measure
      conversions from ad clicks. The LinkedIn Insight Tag sets
      <span class="font-mono text-xs">li_fat_id</span> (30 days) for conversion
      measurement and ad targeting. Google and LinkedIn may additionally set
      cookies on their own domains when their tags load; those follow the
      privacy policies of Google Ireland Ltd and LinkedIn Ireland Unlimited
      Company.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We use Google Consent Mode version 2. Until you consent, all Google tags
      are told that storage is denied and no marketing or analytics cookies are
      set.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Hosting and technical logs</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Our sites are hosted on DigitalOcean in the European Union. Like every
      web server, ours writes technical logs that include IP addresses, used
      only for security and troubleshooting and deleted on rotation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Managing cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You can change your decision here at any time. Clicking the button
      removes your stored choice and the banner will ask you again.
    </p>
    <button type="button" onclick="window.__gcResetConsent()" class="mt-4 rounded-full bg-gray-950 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-gray-800">
      Change my cookie choice
    </button>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You can also delete or block cookies in your browser settings at any
      time. Blocking essential cookies will keep the app from signing you in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-950">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Mail us at join@growcentric.ai and a human answers, usually within one
      business day. When this policy changes, the date at the top changes with
      it.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
